# Provenance: licensing-capability-matrix.yml run 35240608290 (2026-09-17),
# 2020.3.49f1 / personal, via the CLI's own `activate` against a real project.
# Trimmed to the licensing lines; access tokens are masked as Unity masks them.
#
# Nothing here is granted: the licence update is refused by the server, and the
# editor says so in as many words. It is nevertheless the log that was almost
# read as a success twice over:
#
#   - "Successfully resolved entitlements" only means the query reached Unity's
#     server, not that anything was found. #290 fixed exactly this false
#     positive, which is why the grader must require the assignment line.
#   - "Activation complete." is the script's own line, printed after the
#     editor had already said "No valid Unity Editor license found." A grader
#     that trusts the script's summary line is grading the bug.
#
# "No license activation found for this computer" is scoped to the machine, and
# is the same failure the account produced on every version while its seats were
# exhausted - not something specific to 2020.3.
